":{"input_tokens":134677,"output_tokens":2479,"requests":5}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Either add an explicit assertion to test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py that _scanner-integration.yml is reachable specifically from the gerrit-verify.yaml local-uses closure, or re-attribute AC #4 to the test that actually proves the Gerrit scanner job wiring (e.g. the inverted test_ci_workflow_parity / test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment assertions).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC #4: 'pytest tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py proves the auto-running scanner reusable is reachable from the Gerrit Verified workflow closure'","Plan Testing: '... and the scanner reusable is present in the predates local-uses closure'","test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py asserts only `set(GUARDED_WORKFLOWS) <= derived` and `.github/workflows/_artifact-probe.yml in derived` (lines 182-186, 257-268); no reference to _scanner-integration.yml anywhere in the file","_WORKFLOW_GUARD_ROOTS is a union over gerrit-verify.yaml and test.yml (lines 74-77); test.yml already calls _scanner-integration.yml (test_code_review_ws5.py line 954), so the reusable is already in the derived closure via test.yml"],"finding":"AC #4 and the Testing section attribute to test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py a proof it does not make: that the auto-running scanner reusable is reachable from the Gerrit Verified workflow closure. The current test asserts only `set(GUARDED_WORKFLOWS) <= derived` and `_artifact-probe.yml in derived`; it names no scanner path, and its closure is a union rooted at both gerrit-verify.yaml AND test.yml, where test.yml already calls _scanner-integration.yml. The test therefore passes identically whether or not the scanner job is added to gerrit-verify.yaml and cannot distinguish Gerrit-lane reachability. The plan does not enumerate an edit adding this assertion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0745b1450b91fd7d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria bullet 4 / Testing section (test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py)","norm_id":"nf03563d0c7c42718","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer runs the named test expecting it to prove Gerrit-lane scanner reachability, but it stays green even if the scanner job were never added to gerrit-verify.yaml"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Close the job-level gap in the advisory guarantee: either make the vote normalization explicitly tolerate a non-success `scanner-integration` job (so its result is never folded into the Verified cast while advisory), or document/constrain the scanner job (no long `timeout-minutes`, note that concurrency-cancellation of the advisory job must not gate) — and narrow AC-2's claim from 'even on checkout/setup/install failures' to the failure modes step-level continue-on-error actually covers.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gerrit-verify.yaml line 446 aggregates via im-open/workflow-conclusion; vote.CONCLUSION (lines 477-504) trusts env.WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION when the NAMED needs are all success, but the advisory scanner job is deliberately absent from that named set","gerrit-verify.yaml line 54 sets `cancel-in-progress: true`, so a superseding patchset can leave the scanner job `cancelled` (a job-level, not step-level, conclusion)","GHA semantics: `continue-on-error` on a step only prevents that STEP from failing the job; a job timeout / cancellation / reusable-call error still concludes the job non-success regardless of step-level flags","AC line 2 asserts the advisory caller 'cannot cast Verified -1 through WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION even on checkout/setup/install failures' — accurate for step failures, overclaimed for job-level cancellation/timeout"],"finding":"Step-level `continue-on-error: ${{ inputs.advisory-mode }}` neutralizes STEP failures but not JOB-level non-success conclusions (timeout-minutes expiry, concurrency cancellation, or a reusable-workflow call/input-validation error); such a job-level failure/cancellation of the advisory scanner would still fold into `WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION` and could cast Verified -1 on an otherwise-green full route — the exact anti-90c7 class the plan targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3a13a857dad9b75b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (advisory-mode continue-on-error design) and Acceptance Criteria line 2","norm_id":"nd154ce26970c91cd","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A newer patchset arrives mid-run and cancels the scanner job while build-and-test etc. finish green -> WORKFLOW_CONCLUSION becomes cancelled -> Verified -1 on a change whose real gates all passed","The scanner reusable call errors o